":true,"one":"fresh cilantro"}],"steps":[{"text":"Mix the chicken with the yogurt, half the garam masala, the grated garlic and the salt. Marinate in the fridge for at least {time 30 min notimer}, or up to overnight.","uses":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"text":"Heat the broiler with a rack about {len 6 in} from the heat. Spread the chicken on a foil-lined baking sheet and broil, turning once, until charred in spots, {time 10-12 min}. It will finish in the sauce.","uses":[]},{"text":"Melt the butter in the skillet over medium heat. Cook the onion until soft and golden, {time 8-10 min}. Add the garlic, ginger, cumin, paprika, turmeric, cayenne and the rest of the garam masala and stir for {time 1 min}.","uses":[5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12]},{"text":"Add the tomato sauce and salt and simmer, stirring, until thick and darker, {time 10 min}. Stir in the cream.","uses":[13,14,15]},{"text":"Add the chicken and its juices and simmer gently until cooked through, {time 8-10 min}. The thickest piece should read {temp 165F internal}. Scatter with cilantro and serve with rice or naan.","uses":[16]}]}